From: helmfile-enhancement-plan
Subject: [PATCH] PR-T-12 — CI lint: test-* jobs must contain assertions

Closes G12 (test-named jobs that don't actually test).
Branch: chore/test-name-lint
Depends-on: PR-T-01

Adds .test-name-lint.sh used by the L1 CI step (PR-T-01 already calls it).
Asserts every test-*-job.yaml contains at least one of:
  assert | fail | exit 1 | grep -q

If a job is named `test-*` but doesn't, it's a misnamed setup job and
must be renamed (the catalog of which is in 06_TESTING_STRATEGY.md §3.3).

---
 atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/.test-name-lint.sh | 26 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/.test-name-lint.sh

diff --git a/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/.test-name-lint.sh b/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/.test-name-lint.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..eeeeeee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/.test-name-lint.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# .test-name-lint.sh
+# Enforces: every test-*-job.yaml contains at least one assertion-like token.
+# Authored by helmfile_enhancement_plan/PR-T-12 (2026-05-11).
+set -euo pipefail
+
+SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
+cd "${SCRIPT_DIR}"
+
+status=0
+for f in test-*-job.yaml; do
+  [ -e "$f" ] || continue
+  if ! grep -qE 'assert|fail|exit 1|grep -q|--for=condition' "$f"; then
+    echo "::error file=$f:: $f is named test-* but contains no assertion (PR-T-12)"
+    status=1
+  fi
+done
+
+if [ "$status" -eq 0 ]; then
+  echo "OK: every test-*-job.yaml contains at least one assertion"
+fi
+exit $status
